    <div class="privacy-policy">
        <h1>Thintry Microblogging Social Media - Community Guidelines</h1>
        <p>Hello Thintry Community,</p>

        <p>Welcome to Thintry, a microblogging social media platform that fosters meaningful connections and engaging
            discussions. To ensure a safe, respectful, and enjoyable environment for all users, we have established
            these Community Guidelines. Please read and abide by these guidelines to create a positive experience for
            yourself and others.</p>

        <ol>
            <li><strong>Respectful Interaction:</strong> Treat every member of the Thintry community with respect and
                kindness. Do not engage in any form of harassment, hate speech, personal attacks, or discrimination
                based on race, gender, religion, nationality, or any other characteristic. We encourage diverse
                perspectives and healthy debates, but always maintain a respectful tone.</li>
            <li><strong>Content Integrity:</strong> Share accurate and truthful information. Do not spread false
                information, rumors, or engage in misleading activities. Misinformation can harm the community and
                undermine trust. If you're unsure about the accuracy of something, refrain from sharing it.</li>
            <li><strong>No Offensive Content:</strong> Do not post or share explicit, adult, violent, or offensive
                content. Thintry is a platform for all ages, and content that may be considered inappropriate or
                offensive to a general audience is not allowed.</li>
            <li><strong>Intellectual Property:</strong> Respect copyright and intellectual property rights. Do not post
                content that you do not have the rights to or that violates someone else's intellectual property. Always
                give proper credit when sharing content from other sources.</li>
            <li><strong>Privacy and Personal Information:</strong> Protect your own privacy and the privacy of others.
                Do not share personal information such as addresses, phone numbers, or financial information. Obtain
                consent before sharing someone else's personal information.</li>
            <li><strong>No Spam or Self-Promotion:</strong> Avoid spamming the platform with excessive self-promotion,
                advertisements, or unrelated content. Thintry is about authentic engagement, so focus on meaningful
                interactions rather than pushing products or services.</li>
            <li><strong>Reporting and Moderation:</strong> If you come across content that violates these guidelines or
                observe any suspicious activity, please report it to our moderation team. They will review and take
                appropriate action.</li>
            <li><strong>Use of Thintry Brand:</strong> Do not use the Thintry logo, name, or any other branding elements
                in a way that could cause confusion or imply endorsement without our explicit permission.</li>
            <li><strong>Be Mindful of Your Influence:</strong> As an active member of the Thintry community, your words
                and actions have an impact. Use your influence to contribute positively and constructively to
                discussions.</li>
            <li><strong>Continuous Improvement:</strong> We value your feedback. If you have suggestions, concerns, or
                ideas to improve Thintry's community experience, feel free to reach out to us at <a
                    href="mailto:connect@thintry.com">connect@thintry.com</a>.</li>
        </ol>

        <p>Failure to adhere to these Community Guidelines may result in warnings, content removal, temporary
            suspension, or permanent account suspension, depending on the severity of the violation. Our aim is to
            create a welcoming and vibrant community, and your cooperation is essential to achieving this goal.</p>

        <p>Thank you for being a part of the Thintry community. Let's work together to make this platform a space where
            everyone feels valued and respected.</p>

        <p>Best regards,</p>
        <p>The Thintry Team</p>
